    {
      "id": 185061,
      "name": "Foote",
      "username": "Foote",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-11-18T16:00:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>It is possible that her quote in Mystery Comics #281, while attributed on the card&nbsp;as who we know today as Fanatic, was said by Helena as a kid before her accident and before she actually became Fanatic. This would keep intact a \"first apperance\" 87 entire issues later.</p><p>Along the same lines, there is speculation out there that Apostate indeed has quotes attributed to him before he was actually known as Apostate. I think, in the comic world, he was an unknown mysterious player for a number of issues before he was formally introduced as Apostate. Even though quotes on cards attribute text to Apostate before his first apperance.</p>",
      "post_number": 9,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:10:30.860Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
